# WCHRT.KEY - the key script of the frame chrome's test, TEST/WCHRT.C;
# every mode of Windows writes TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WCHRT.SNP, which
# TEST/chrtchk.py checks.  The frame: the tool bar
# "New|Open|Edit|Delete|-|Move|Install|Lend|-|*|Find" with an Edit in its
# 80-pixel slot, the Edit that holds the focus but while a drag of the
# splitter is held, the Static "SEEN n CMD c CODE k" (the frame's
# WM_COMMANDs, the last one's wParam and notification code), the Static
# "ANS ..." (the last answer of the bars' API or the splitter's state),
# the status bar of one panel and the splitter in a row of its own.
# Under the splitter's row the preview panel (SRC/WIN/WPREV.H), empty at
# first, down to the status bar.
# The program takes each function key and CTRL letter from its loop, so
# none reaches the focus.
S START
# A click on Open; New let go below it; Lend dragged off and back.
K F2
S CLICK
K CTRL-F2
S DRAGOFF
K F3
S DRAGBACK
# Edit and Delete grayed: a click on Edit sends nothing until it is
# enabled again.
K F4
S GRAY
K SHIFT-F2
S GRAYCLK
K SHIFT-F4
S UNGRAY
K SHIFT-F2
S EDITCLK
# The slot's Edit notifying the bar goes to the frame as it was sent; a
# click on the bar between its buttons sends nothing and takes no focus.
K F5
S FORWARD
K SHIFT-F5
S BARCLK
# Buttons 7 (Find, after the slot) and 8 (none); the slot cut to 40
# pixels; Open still clicks, and Find, after the slot.
K CTRL-F3
S BUTTONS
K SHIFT-F3
S SLOT40
K F2
S CLICK2
K CTRL-F5
S FINDCLK
# One panel: a 100-byte text kept whole in the last panel; no panel 3.
K SHIFT-F8
S S1LONG
K F8
S S1NOP3
# Four panels: panel 0's text cut to a panel's room; the texts set, a
# TAB in one made a space, no panel 4, panel 1 emptied, the 100 bytes
# cut to the last panel's room, then to panel 0's; no fifth panel.
K F6
S S4
K F7
S S4TEXT
K SHIFT-F7
S S4TAB
K CTRL-F7
S S4NOP4
K CTRL-SHIFT-F7
S S4NULL
K F8
S S4LAST
K SHIFT-F8
S S4CELL
K CTRL-F6
S S4NOP5
# Two panels drop the last two, so F7 sets two; four again add two
# empty ones.
K SHIFT-F6
S S2
K F7
S S2TEXT
K F6
S S4AGAIN
# One panel again: panel 0 kept; no bar of no panels; the last panel's
# room back for the 100 bytes.
K CTRL-SHIFT-F6
S S1AGAIN
K ALT-F6
S S0NOP
K SHIFT-F8
S S1LONG2
# Narrow, the slot's Edit lies outside the bar; wide again, inside.
K F9
S NARROW
K SHIFT-F9
S WIDE
# A press on Open that loses its capture never acts.  Open grayed while
# pressed comes up and lets the capture go; its glyph's point is black,
# grayed dark grey; the bar told to cancel its mode lets Open up so; a
# release while the frame is disabled sends nothing.  A double click on
# Open is two clicks, the focus kept.
K CTRL-F4
S PRESSGRY
K CTRL-F8
S PIXEL
K CTRL-SHIFT-F4
S CANCEL
K CTRL-F9
S OWNEROFF
K CTRL-SHIFT-F9
S DBLCLK
# The splitter dragged right, its limits set and it dragged past each,
# held there; dragged away and back, nothing sent.  A drag held open
# has the mouse and the focus, its guide drawn where the pointer is and
# nowhere else; ESC cancels it, the guide gone and the focus back, so a
# release then does nothing; WM_CANCELMODE cancels as ESC does; a
# disabled splitter takes no press; a double click is a press.
K F1
S SPDRAG
K SHIFT-F1
S SPMAX
K CTRL-F1
S SPMIN
K CTRL-SHIFT-F1
S SPSAME
K CTRL-G
S SPMID
K ESC
S SPESC
K CTRL-U
S SPESCUP
K CTRL-K
S SPCANCEL
K CTRL-B
S SPGRAY
K ALT-F1
S SPDBL
# The preview panel.  Its text; its fields and notes in the text's
# place, those too long cut, shown from the first with a scroll bar, as
# they do not fit; no focus rectangle until a click gives it the focus.
K CTRL-T
S PVTEXT
K CTRL-P
S PVFILL
K CTRL-R
S PVPLAIN
M 107 DOWN MID
M 107 UP MID
S PVCLICK
K CTRL-R
S PVFOCUS
# With the focus it scrolls by its keys and to its thumb, within its
# rows; any other key is its owner's, as a double click is ENTER, but
# SHIFT and CTRL alone, which go nowhere.
K DOWN
S PVDOWN
K PGDN
S PVPGDN
K END
S PVEND
K DOWN
S PVLAST
K UP
S PVUP
K PGUP
S PVPGUP
K HOME
S PVHOME
K UP
S PVFIRST
K CTRL-H
S PVTHUMB
K ENTER
S PVENTER
K ESC
S PVESC
K TAB
S PVTAB
M 107 DBL MID
S PVDBL
K CTRL-M
S PVMODS
# Narrow, its values and notes take more rows, and the thumb stays in
# range; wide again, as many as before.
K END F9
S PVNARROW
K SHIFT-F9
S PVWIDE
# Its block takes as many fields of 64 bytes as fill it and no more,
# and two fewer after a field of 65, a byte short of one more; emptied,
# it shows nothing and its text again.
K CTRL-L
S PVCAP
K CTRL-SHIFT-L
S PVCAPODD
K CTRL-T
S PVTEXT2
